; 11:14; Joh 5:24; 6:63,68; 13:20; 17:8,20; Ro 10:17,18; 2Co 5:18 2Pe 3:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-10-23","title":"Acts 10:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>and lodged. Ge 19:2,3; 24:31,32; Jud 19:19-21; Heb 13:2; 1Pe 4:9 on. 29,33; Ec 9:10 and certain. 45; 9:38,42; 11:12; 2Co 8:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-10-24","title":"Acts 10:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>the morrow. 9 Cesarea.This city, once an obscure fortress called Strato's Tower, was built and superbly decorated by Herod the Great and called C�sarea, in honour of Augustus C�sar, to whom he dedicated it in the 28th year of his reign. It was situated on the shore of the Mediterranean, between Joppa and Dora, with a haven, rendered by Herod the most convenient on the coast: according to Ibn Idris and Abulfeda, 30 miles from Jaffa or Joppa, 32 from Ramlay, and 36 from Acco or Ptolemais; and, according to Josephus, 600 stadia, or 75 miles from Jerusalem, though the real distance is probably not more than 62 miles. Nothing now remains of the former splendour of C�sarea: the supposed sites of the ancient edifices are mere mounds of indefinable form; the waves wash the ruins of the mole, the tower, and the port; the whole of the surrounding country is a sandy desert; and not a creature except beasts of prey, resides within many miles of this silent desolation.</p>\n<p>and had. Isa 2:3; Mic 4:2; Zec 3:10; 8:20-23; Mt 9:9,10; Mr 5:19,20; Lu 5:29 Joh 1:41-49; 4:28,29; 1:1-3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-10-25","title":"Acts 10:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>and fell. 14:11-13; Da 2:30,46; Mt 8:2; 14:33; Re 19:10; 22:8,9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-10-26","title":"Acts 10:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>Stand. 14:14,15; Isa 42:8; 48:13; Mt 4:10; 2Th 2:3,4; Re 13:8; 19:10; 22:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-10-27","title":"Acts 10:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>and found. 24; 14:27; Joh 4:35; 1Co 16:9; 2Co 2:12; Col 4:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-10-28","title":"Acts 10:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>that it. 11:2,3; 22:21,22; Joh 4:9,27; 18:28; Ga 2:12-14 but. 15,34; 11:9; 15:8,9; Isa 65:5; Lu 18:11; Eph 3:6,7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-10-29","title":"Acts 10:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>as soon. 19,20; Ps 119:60; 1Pe 3:15 I ask. 21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-10-30","title":"Acts 10:30","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":30,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":30},"content":"<p>Four. 7-9,23,24 I was. 3; Ezr 9:4,5; Ne 9:1-3; Da 9:20,21 and, behold. 1:10; Mt 28:3; Mr 16:6; Lu 24:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-10-31","title":"Acts 10:31","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":31,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":31},"content":"<p>thy. Isa 38:5; Da 9:23; 10:12; Lu 1:13 are. 4; Le 2:2,9; 5:12; Php 4:18; Heb 6:10; Re 5:8; 8:3,4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-10-32","title":"Acts 10:32","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":32,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":32},"content":"<p>therefore. 5-8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-10-33","title":"Acts 10:33","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":33,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":33},"content":"<p>are we. 17:11,12; 28:28; De 5:25-29; 2Ch 30:12; Pr 1:5; 9:9,10; 18:15; 25:12 Mt 18:4; 